course: dictionary
lesson: 13992
title: One word, two meanings: loom
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and loom is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «The children wove a scarf on the old wooden loom.» Here a loom is a machine or frame for weaving thread into cloth, because the words weave and scarf are clues.
explain: Now look at this sentence: «A huge shape loomed out of the thick fog.» Loomed is a verb here. The clues are huge, out of the fog, and shape: something large and dark is slowly appearing. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Loom can also mean something is about to happen, often something worrying. «Our spelling test looms on Friday, so I must start revising.» The clues are on Friday and must start revising: the test is coming soon and it is a little worrying. When someone says a problem looms large, it means it seems very important or worrying.
fact: A loom is a machine or frame for weaving thread into cloth.
fact: As a verb, «loom» means to appear as a large, dark, unclear shape, often in a frightening way.
fact: «Loom» can also mean to seem about to happen, especially something worrying or important.
fact: «Loom large» means to seem very important or worrying.
fact: Power looms in mills changed how cloth was made during the Industrial Revolution.
exercise: «The children wove a scarf on the small wooden loom.» What is a loom here? | A bird that sings at dawn | *A frame for weaving thread into cloth | A tall tree in the garden | A dark cloud over the sea
exercise: «A huge shape loomed out of the thick fog.» What does loomed mean? | Fell to the ground | *Appeared as a large, dark, unclear shape | Ran away quickly | Shouted loudly
exercise: «Our spelling test looms on Friday, so I must start revising.» What does looms mean? | Is very quiet and small | Turns into a bird | Goes away for good | *Seems about to happen soon
test: «The tall castle loomed over the village.» What does loomed suggest? | It stood far away and looked small | *It appeared large and dark, looking powerful or frightening | It was being built that week | It fell down slowly
test: Mum says, «The science fair looms large this term.» What does loom large mean? | *It seems very important or worrying | It has been cancelled | It gets smaller and disappears | It is in the garden
exam: Which meaning fits «The mill's loom wove cloth all day»? | *A machine for weaving thread into cloth | Seemed about to happen | Shouted in fear | Appeared as a dark shape
